This discussion is too arcane for me :) , but I can live with that.

In the meantime, I think my fix would be just to convert the factor to character and then back:

> d <- data.table(name = c('a','b','c'), value = 1:3)
> dt <- data.table(d)
> setkey(dt,'name')
> dt1 <- subset(dt,name != 'a')  # or dt1 <- dt[ name != 'a' ]
> dt1
     name value
[1,]    b     2
[2,]    c     3
> droplevels(dt1) # ouch
     name value
[1,]    b     1
[2,]    c     3
> 
> # A cheap fix
> dt1$name<-factor(as.character(dt1$name))
> setkey(dt1,name)
> dt1
     name value
[1,]    b     2
[2,]    c     3
>


